{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,15.359,1.643,1.471,"India Equity Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"19 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,33.711,3.651,3.268,"Punjab National Bank"],[13.889,14.731,36.681,2.373,2.124,"Margins turn up; the price got there first"],[13.889,20.845,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Punjab National Bank’s Q2 FY27 net profit rose 12.8% to ₹5,532 cr, and the"],[13.889,22.289,52.957,1.809,1.634,"shares have gained 29% since the results on 16 October (NIFTY: 9%) and now"],[13.889,23.733,52.931,1.809,1.634,"sit above all 18 broker targets (highest ₹145, mean ₹130). The profit growth"],[13.889,25.177,52.987,1.809,1.634,"came from provisions. Operating profit rose 4%; provisions fell to ₹97 cr from"],[13.889,26.621,52.934,1.809,1.634,"₹643 cr, as a write-back on IL&FS loans (₹1,200-1,300 cr, per the call) paid for"],[13.889,28.065,52.931,1.809,1.634,"an extra ₹1,150 cr set aside for the new loss rules. Lending did improve: the"],[13.889,29.509,52.931,1.809,1.634,"margin rose 8 bp in the quarter to 2.58%, net interest income grew 11% and"],[13.889,30.954,50.439,1.809,1.634,"loans 15%. Treasury income fell 57% as bond yields rose; staff costs fell 7%."],[13.889,33.439,52.992,1.809,1.634,"1) Rates help first: over half of loans track the repo rate and repriced the day"],[13.889,34.883,52.931,1.809,1.634,"after the 25 bp rise. We take the margin from 2.59% in FY27E to 2.68% in"],[13.889,36.328,52.966,1.809,1.634,"FY28E; net interest income grows 12% and 16%. 2) Other income shrinks:"],[13.889,37.772,52.934,1.809,1.634,"written-off recoveries and treasury gains, 57% of it in FY26, are fading. 3)"],[13.889,39.216,52.951,1.809,1.634,"Expected-credit-loss rules start in April 2027: of the bank’s ₹8,000 cr estimate,"],[13.889,40.684,52.931,1.809,1.634,"₹1,150 cr is provided; we charge the rest to reserves (₹6 a share) and lift loan"],[13.889,42.128,52.966,1.809,1.634,"provisions to 0.45% of loans in FY28E from 0.25% in H1. 4) The pay deal"],[13.889,43.572,52.934,1.809,1.634,"expires in October 2027; we add ₹2,700 cr a year. Group EPS before one-offs"],[13.889,45.016,22.253,1.809,1.634,"grows 12% in FY27E, then is flat."],[13.889,47.502,52.934,1.809,1.634,"Our Dec-27 target of ₹145 averages two methods that disagree. A sum of parts"],[13.889,48.946,52.954,1.809,1.634,"gives ₹170: the bank at 1.1x book (₹156), on a 12% cost of equity and a 12.5%"],[13.889,50.39,52.936,1.809,1.634,"long-run return on book, plus PNB Housing, the rural banks and other stakes at"],[13.889,51.834,52.936,1.809,1.634,"market value less 20% (₹14). PNB’s three-year average P/E of 6.0x gives ₹123;"],[13.889,53.278,52.934,1.809,1.634,"the shares trade at 7.3x. The price assumes an 11.6% long-run return. If returns"],[13.889,54.722,52.951,1.809,1.634,"hold at 14% under the new rules, the target rises to ₹165; at 11% it falls to ₹130."],[13.889,56.167,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Risks: farm loans (8.6% bad), and lower bond yields, which would raise pension"],[13.889,57.611,3.717,1.809,1.634,"costs."],[13.889,60.098,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[15.758,68.709,0.999,1.022,0.915,"80"],[15.268,66.942,1.489,1.022,0.915,"100"],[15.268,65.174,1.489,1.022,0.915,"120"],[15.268,63.407,1.489,1.022,0.915,"140"],[15.268,61.639,1.489,1.022,0.915,"160"],[18.061,69.404,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Jan 26"],[22.684,69.404,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Apr 26"],[27.471,69.404,2.47,1.022,0.915,"Jul 26"],[32.243,69.404,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[19.051,70.575,2.417,1.275,1.111,"PNB ("],[21.471,70.601,0.618,1.241,1.111,"₹"],[22.084,70.575,0.303,1.275,1.111,")"],[25.168,70.575,7.901,1.275,1.111,"NIFTY 50 (rebased)"],[20.291,71.735,1.972,1.387,1.209,"YTD"],[25.561,71.735,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[30.279,71.735,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.446,71.735,1.984,1.387,1.209,"12m"],[15.277,72.8,1.691,1.387,1.209,"Abs"],[19.372,72.8,2.811,1.387,1.209,"24.6%"],[24.09,72.8,2.811,1.387,1.209,"2